## Last-arg vs token walk (Decide card)
| | Token-stream (`c_secret_scan_call` sys_exec) | C-text last (`c_sys_exec_last_arg`) |
|--|----------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|
| Input | Lexer toks (`IDENT` field 3) | Lowered joined C `args` string |
| Span | every argv after cap (`want=1`, `eq_only=false`) | **last** top-level comma span only |
| When | check + emit-c + llvm IDENT walk | `c_secret_emit_guard` sys_exec after lower |
| Quote comma | Impossible (not IDENT) | Must skip `"…"` / `\\` or last_start drifts |
| Nested `,` | Tok depth / COMMA | Must use `depth` on `(`/`)` |
| Heap | Token list already paid | O(\|args\|) char_at + **one slice** (7.2 claim) |
| Path-A job | Mid-argv + last IDENT | Belt if last bare IDENT after lower |
| 7.2 residual | Not the CRIT | **This is the CRIT** (concat fear + unproved skip) |

**Ship-now decision:** keep **both**. Close 7.2 on the last-arg walker’s **slice + quote/depth prove**. Mid-argv stays token-walk. Unification = later (I7), not a substitute for I1.

