## Top recommendation (this turn — path-A residual close)
### **Ship: Prove/close 7.2 (I1) + quote/depth edge matrix (I2). Optionally land ident-slice helper (I3) on 7.10 same wave.**
**Why this closes 7.2:**
- Walker is already the Path-A fix (`str_slice`, no per-char OoStr). SPRINT “same” as 7.1 stack-buffer wording is a **wrong tool**.
- Unclosed part is **untested quote/depth + untested claim** (\(U\)): last IDENT/lit fixtures exist; **quote-comma and nested-depth do not**.
- Mid-argv refuse is **not** last-arg’s job; smoke must keep `secret_sys_exec_argv_fail` on the token rail so we do not fake-close via last-span.
- Shared ident helper is the right **7.10** close using the **7.1/7.2** pattern — not a 7.2 rewrite.

### DE winner advice (plain English)
1. **Do not rewrite** `c_sys_exec_last_arg` into tokens, ident-slice, or a C `char[]`.
2. **Prove static:** in `c_emit_args.oo` `c_sys_exec_last_arg`, last-span materialization is `str_slice` only (L121–129).
3. **Wire smoke (I2):** new `scripts/s72_last_arg_smoke.oo` (preferred; s71 TMPDIR shape) **or** extend `secret_sink_enforce_smoke.oo`. Minimum:
   - existing `secret_sys_exec_fail` REFUSE
   - existing `secret_sys_exec_pass` ALLOW
   - existing `secret_sys_exec_argv_fail` REFUSE (dual-path honesty)
   - TMPDIR quote-comma ALLOW
   - TMPDIR quote-comma + last IDENT REFUSE
   - TMPDIR nested `helper(a, b)` last ALLOW
4. **SPRINT 7.2:** mark FIXED path-A **only after** smoke exit 0 on rebuilt host. Replace “same” wording.
5. **If same-wave budget:** I3 `c_ident_end` / `c_slice_ident_at` → rewrite **7.10** `c_parse_secret_env` name loop to one slice. Leave last-arg as-is.
6. **Done bar:**
   - Last argv SECRET IDENT **does** refuse (`ERR\tsecret`).
   - Last argv string lit with unused SECRET name **does not** refuse.
   - Comma inside a C string does **not** steal `last_start`.
   - Comma inside nested `(` `)` does **not** steal `last_start`.
   - Grep: no per-char last-span concat in `c_sys_exec_last_arg`.
   - Mid-argv / nested-call-inner IDENT / interp / IFC remain **named residual** if not already on token walk.
7. **Out of scope:** I6 full argv C-text scan; I7 emit tok plumbing; I8 C buffer; I9 lattice; I10 blind split; I5 drop-first unless quote smoke proves emit split.

